  "sections": [
    {
      "tone": "dark",
      "kicker": "SPECIAL REPORT / THE NOVELTY AND NUISANCE DESK",
      "heading": "Glitter bomb cards: a study in disappointment.\n(Loud on the box. Quiet on the porch.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "runs": [
            {
              "text": "The "
            },
            {
              "text": "Institute for Alarming Conclusions",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " tested 500 screaming glitter bomb cards under laboratory conditions, which is to say on a porch, in a mailbox, and in one case a very patient drawer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "runs": [
            {
              "text": "The findings are in. Glitter bomb cards are "
            },
            {
              "text": "extremely effective at being purchased.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " They are "
            },
            {
              "text": "less effective at everything after that.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " Researchers identified the three leading weaknesses: "
            },
            {
              "text": "a card that must be opened, a victim who must open it,",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " and "
            },
            {
              "text": "a victim who must not have read the front.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " "
            },
            {
              "text": "All three are, at present, outside the card's control.",
              "italic": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "runs": [
            {
              "text": "A glitter bomb is the only weapon that needs "
            },
            {
              "text": "the victim's participation, a free hand, and a good mood.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " It also needs the scream to go off "
            },
            {
              "text": "while the victim is still standing there.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " "
            },
            {
              "text": "The packaging promises up to 30 seconds of screaming. The Institute recorded a drawer, a year later, and a very surprised cat.",
              "italic": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "runs": [
            {
              "text": "Sound is the weak point. The scream is produced by "
            },
            {
              "text": "a chip the size of a cough drop",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " and a battery with "
            },
            {
              "text": "a very strong sense of its own timing.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " "
            },
            {
              "text": "The battery is the only part of the card that screams on schedule, and it is always the wrong schedule.",
              "italic": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "runs": [
            {
              "text": "As for the glitter: "
            },
            {
              "text": "once released, glitter cannot be recalled.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " It is the Pyro Posse's only reliable follow-through. "
            },
            {
              "text": "The Institute expects it to outlast the card, the prank, the party, and several grudges.",
              "italic": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "runs": [
            {
              "text": "The Institute's final recommendation: "
            },
            {
              "text": "the best glitter bomb is the one that never ships.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " The second best is "
            },
            {
              "text": "the one opened by someone who read the front.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " "
            },
            {
              "text": "The pink team has been informed, and has already finished its cookies.",
              "italic": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "cta",
          "label": "See what the card left behind →",
          "href": "https://purrpetrators.net/cases/008/",
          "note": "The evidence is on the site, not in this email. The cookies are not included."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tone": "white",
      "heading": "The numbers, such as they are",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "stats",
          "items": [
            {
              "value": "4%",
              "text": "**Glitter bomb cards that scream on cue.** The other 96% scream *in a drawer, in a mailbox, or after the recipient has politely left the room.*"
            },
            {
              "value": "100%",
              "text": "**Glitter that is still somewhere.** *Couch cushions, car seats, one sandwich.* PNN's cleanup desk expects full recovery in three to five business years."
            },
            {
              "value": "88%",
              "text": "**Glitter bombs defused by someone who read the front first.** The other 12% were defused by someone who read the front second."
            },
            {
              "value": "87%",
              "text": "**Adults who can spell 'strategy' on a calm, quiet day.** Under pressure, poster deadlines, or fire: **61%.** The rest go with *'stratogy,' 'stratigy,' or a confident 'plan.'*"
            },
            {
              "value": "3 of 4",
              "text": "**Typos noticed only after the poster is printed.** The fourth was noticed by the pink team, at a glance. *Sources describe the glance as brief, and unbothered.*"
            },
            {
              "value": "52%",
              "text": "**Adults who have confidently typed 'definately,' felt a flicker, and sent it anyway.** *The flicker was the correct spelling, trying to get your attention.*"
            },
            {
              "value": "9 of 10",
              "text": "**Adults who can spell 'Purrpetrators' on the first try.** *The Pyro Posse is among them. Which means 'stratogy' was a choice. PNN respects choices.*"
            },
            {
              "value": "0",
              "text": "**Times a screaming card has been improved by a typo.** *The typo was louder.*"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "runs": [
            {
              "text": "Lead finding:",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " adults spell beautifully when nobody is watching and terribly when everybody is. The word 'strategy' is a known trap: it looks easy right up until it isn't. "
            },
            {
              "text": "PNN's editors proofread this entire newsletter three times. A fourth pass is scheduled for after Clueso finishes the first.",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " The poster in question is on file as "
            },
            {
              "text": "Exhibit F",
              "bold": true,
              "href": "https://purrpetrators.net/cases/008/"
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
